From 682516f085b20e5b7f023088682dc2ce663897af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 23:23:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] orchestration: cargo specs without Node stand-ins for
 the decision API

- The decision API stub runs in the test process; decision-stub.mjs is gone.
- The QuickJS async-context spec runs on the real bundle in cargo instead of
  an esbuild lowering in vitest (esbuild leaves the dev dependencies). It
  caught the for-await lowering bug fixed in the previous commit.
- Specs whose rules the cargo specs already cover are removed: the Node
  import rejection at the bundle layer, skip/fail on a throwing jssg file in
  vitest, and resuming an unfinalized history in vitest.

Test lines since the port: +317 -> +216. Vitest 614 -> 609 specs,
7.06 s -> 6.31 s. Cargo 119 specs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
